                <pb facs="1165" n="1155" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg1155"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.9533/12–2749: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Second Secretary of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bacon</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-12-27">December 27, 1949.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 27—1:13 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2664. Sent Department, repeated Shanghai 1302, Tsingtao unnumbered.</p>
                <p>“Situation unchanged. Hawthorne.”</p>
                <p>(Re Embtel 2636 to Dept, repeated Shanghai 1290, December 21.<anchor n="27"
                        xml:id="d1467-f1"/>)</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bacon</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>[The Consulate General at Tsingtao was officially closed on January 23, 1950,
                        at the time of the departure of the American personnel.]</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
